     That's exactly right.  He's not asleep, so noise doesn't
matter.  He'll come out of his meditation when he can see you, or
when his health is less than maximum (which is why pet mind flayers
can wake the Wizard from afar), or when he becomes angry (which
will happen if you attack him even if the attack happens to inflict
no damage).

     Bug C343-187 is relevant here.  In the hypothetical future
post-3.4.3 version, noise will "wake" meditating monsters whether
they can see you or not.

